{
    "map": {
        "attribute_tolerances.descr": "The fields that will be compared to determine if they are within a tolerance. The tolerance value is a value in the units of the attribute.",
        "attribute_tolerances.dt.title1": "Field",
        "attribute_tolerances.dt.title2": "Tolerance",
        "attribute_tolerances.title": "Attribute Tolerance",
        "compare_status.title": "Compare Status",
        "compare_type.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies the type of rasters that will be compared.</p><ul><li><span title=\"RASTER_DATASET\">Raster dataset</span>—Two raster datasets will be compared.</li><li><span title=\"GDB_RASTER_DATASET\">Geodatabase raster dataset</span>—Two raster datasets in a geodatabase will be compared.</li><li><span title=\"MOSAIC_DATASET\">Mosaic dataset</span>—Two mosaic datasets will be compared.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "compare_type.domain.GDB_RASTER_DATASET": "Geodatabase raster dataset",
        "compare_type.domain.MOSAIC_DATASET": "Mosaic dataset",
        "compare_type.domain.RASTER_DATASET": "Raster dataset",
        "compare_type.title": "Compare Type",
        "continue_compare.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies whether the comparison will stop if a mismatch is encountered.</p><ul><li>Unchecked—The comparison will stop if a mismatch is encountered. This is the default.</li><li>Checked—The comparison will continue if a mismatch is encountered.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "continue_compare.title": "Continue Comparison",
        "description": "Compares the properties of two raster datasets or two mosaic datasets.",
        "ignore_option.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies the properties that will be ignored in the comparison.</p><ul><li><span title=\"BandCount\">Band count</span>—The number of bands will be ignored.</li><li><span title=\"Extent\">Extent</span>—The extent will be ignored.</li><li><span title=\"Columns And Rows\">Columns and rows</span>—The number of columns and rows will be ignored.</li><li><span title=\"Pixel Type\">Pixel type</span>—The pixel type will be ignored.</li><li><span title=\"NoData\">NoData</span>—The NoData value will be ignored.</li><li><span title=\"Spatial Reference\">Spatial reference</span>—The spatial reference system will be ignored.</li><li><span title=\"Pixel Value\">Pixel value</span>—The pixel values will be ignored.</li><li><span title=\"Colormap\">Colormap</span>—Existing color maps will be ignored.</li><li><span title=\"Raster Attribute Table\">Raster attribute table</span>—Existing attribute tables will be ignored.</li><li><span title=\"Statistics\">Statistics</span>—Statistics will be ignored.</li><li><span title=\"Metadata\">Metadata</span>—Metadata will be ignored.</li><li><span title=\"Pyramids Exist\">Pyramids exist</span>—Existing pyramids will be ignored.</li><li><span title=\"Compression Type\">Compression type</span>—The compression type will be ignored.</li><li><span title=\"Data Source Type\">Data source type</span>—The data source type will be ignored.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "ignore_option.title": "Ignore Options",
        "in_base_raster.descr": "The first raster or mosaic dataset to compare.",
        "in_base_raster.title": "Input Base Raster",
        "in_test_raster.descr": "The second raster or mosaic dataset to compare with the first.",
        "in_test_raster.title": "Input Test Raster",
        "omit_field.descr": "The field or fields that will be omitted during comparison.",
        "omit_field.title": "Omit Fields",
        "out_compare_file.descr": "A text file containing the comparison results.",
        "out_compare_file.title": "Output Compare File",
        "parameter_tolerances.descr": "<xdoc><p>The tolerances that determine the range in which values are considered equal. The same tolerance can be applied to all parameters, or different tolerances can be applied to individual parameters.</p><p>The tolerance type can be either a value or a fraction.</p><p>If the tolerance type is a fraction, the tolerance for each pixel will be different since each pixel has a different value. For example, if a tolerance fraction is set to 0.5, the tolerance will be calculated as follows:<ul><li>If a pixel has a value of 0.2, the tolerance will be 0.1, since 0.5 * 0.2 = 0.1.</li><li>If a pixel has a value of 3, the tolerance will be 1.5, since 0.5 * 3 = 1.5.</li></ul></p></xdoc>",
        "parameter_tolerances.domain.item1.All": "All",
        "parameter_tolerances.domain.item1.Extent": "Extent",
        "parameter_tolerances.domain.item1.Pixel_Value": "Pixel values",
        "parameter_tolerances.domain.item1.Statistics_Maximum": "Maximum",
        "parameter_tolerances.domain.item1.Statistics_Mean": "Mean",
        "parameter_tolerances.domain.item1.Statistics_Minimum": "Minimum",
        "parameter_tolerances.domain.item1.Statistics_Standard_Deviation": "Standard deviation",
        "parameter_tolerances.domain.item3.Fraction": "Fraction",
        "parameter_tolerances.domain.item3.Value": "Value",
        "parameter_tolerances.dt.title1": "Parameter",
        "parameter_tolerances.dt.title2": "Tolerance",
        "parameter_tolerances.dt.title3": "Type",
        "parameter_tolerances.title": "Parameter Tolerance",
